<!--Post: 6915--><!--Time: 1108074231-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6915"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nm_pi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nm_pi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 2:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->While I was reading about the &#34;Coleman Connection&#34; aspect of this case I had an “OUT-THERE” thought that relates to several murder cases in NM... If interested see: <BR><a href="http://kaitarquette.arquettes.com" target=_top>http://kaitarquette.arquettes.com</a> <BR><a href="http://www.realcrimes.com" target=_top>http://www.realcrimes.com</a> <BR> <BR>I’m sure this theory that I’m about to propose has been discussed before in one form or another, somewhere, but please humor me…. <BR> <BR>Theory: <BR>From what I could gather, the Coleman Factory is located on the railroad tracks.  Based upon research I have conducted, it appears that a great deal of drug trafficking &#40;pot, cocaine, heroin&#41; out of Mexico has occurred along the railroad, especially prior to the NAFTA agreement &#40;1994?&#41; which makes it much easier for trucks containing goods from Mexico to enter the US.  Drugs are brought into the country, off-loaded from the rail cars and promptly stored in Stash Houses, often near the railroad tracks, for subsequent local distribution, as well as being routed to tractor trailers.  From what I gather, nightclubs and bars are popular destination points.  From what I gather, this national distribution network was established in large part during the prohibition era to facilitate the transportation of alchohol.  <BR> <BR>It is well-documented that Mexican drug cartels that initially supported, and then took over for the Colombian Cartels after their demise in the late 80s due to American Miliraty Intervention, have entire networks of law enforcement, judges, lawyers, politicians, and prominent businessmen that are “bought off” in Mexico.  <BR> <BR>In May, 2004, a Chief Judge of Albuquerque was arrested on narcotics charges. Several law enforcement officials in the state have also been implicated on narcotic&#39;s related charges or required to resign.  The media aired information from a confidential narcotics report about drug activities involving, not only the Judge, but numerous other prominent NM judges, attorneys, and members of the state legislature dating back decades. “It draws on a variety of sources and reads like a Who’s Who of New Mexico drug underworld,” the reporter said. “Judges, lawyers, politicians, sports celebrities and prominent businessmen appear in the report right along side the State’s narcotics kingpins.” Now, there are a number of unsolved murders that the victim’s families believe are related knowledge of this drug underworld, and certain police that they believe protect it. &#40;see abovementioned websites&#41;. <BR> <BR>Now, consider the whole Iran-Contra/CIA/Manual Noriega cocaine-for-arms network supposedly in operation during the 80s, and prior to that, the often-alleged Air America, Golden Triangle Operations out of Southeast Asia.  See for example:  <BR> <BR><a href="http://www2.gwu.edu/~nsarchiv/NSAEBB/NSAEBB2/nsaebb2.htm" target=_top>http://www2.gwu.edu/~nsarchiv/NSAEBB/NSAEBB2/nsaeb b2.htm</a> <BR><a href="http://www.ciadrugs.com/index_right_cia.html" target=_top>http://www.ciadrugs.com/index_right_cia.html</a> <BR><a href="http://www.thirdworldtraveler.com/CIA/CIAdrug_fallout.html" target=_top>http://www.thirdworldtraveler.com/CIA/CIAdrug_fall out.html</a> <BR><a href="http://www.a1b2c3.com/drugs/opi007.htm" target=_top>http://www.a1b2c3.com/drugs/opi007.htm</a> <BR><a href="http://www.serendipity.li/cia/blum1.html" target=_top>http://www.serendipity.li/cia/blum1.html</a> <BR> <BR>Questions <BR>1. It appears that the old Coleman Factory is located along a railroad.  Could it have been an off-loading point for large quantities of drugs?   <BR>2. Were these activities protected? <BR>3. Could Joe O. have been covertly tied to, or knowledgeable of, these activities through his military service? <BR>4. Did the victims that worked there become aware of this operation for some reason and have to be silenced?  <BR>5. Was the “BTK Personality” created to cover these hits? <BR>6. Could the Blackout Bar been a destination point for drugs that linked Cheryl to the other victims and “BTK” mistook Shirley for Cheryl and hit her instead? <BR> <BR>In my mind, this outlandish theory could explain some aspects of the case that are troubling me.  Go ahead and rip it apart. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
