<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6923"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Woody<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Woody<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 3:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->My only problem w/ this theory is why in the world would this group of individuals need to reappear now?  If we&#39;re to believe that they created &#34;BTK&#34; in order to cover their tracks, then they succeeded.  They wouldn&#39;t need to make him supposedly appear again; I, like a lot of people, figured he either died, went to prison, or moved on. <BR> <BR>Good post, though!  It would certainly make one helluva movie.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
