<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6949"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tadpole<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tadpole<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 6:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bravo! Well said! One needs to step back and look at what was going on in the US/Central Americas during the 70&#39;s.  American forces trained Central Americans in commando tactics to fight the drug lords. Anti-communism. Drugs. IMO there was a lot of covering up going on that government didn&#39;t want out to the public. Kind of &#34;you cover my back, I&#39;ll cover yours.&#34; <!--/Text--></td></tr>
